  "number": 4,
  "title": "Add /schema endpoint to expose database structure",
  "body": "                                                                                                               \n  Users querying /chat often don't know what tables or columns exist in the connected SQLite database, which     \n  leads to vague questions and poor SQL generation. We should expose a read-only endpoint that returns the\n  database schema so clients (and humans) can discover what's queryable.                                         \n                                                        \n  Requirements:                                                                                                  \n  - Add a new GET /schema endpoint to main.py.\n  - Response should return a JSON object listing each table and its columns (name + type).                       \n  - Use the existing SQLite connection logic — do not introduce a new DB client.          \n  - Handle the case where the database is empty or unreachable with a clear error response.                      \n                                                                                                                 \n  Example response:                                                                                              \n  {                                                                                                              \n    \"tables\": [                                                                                                  \n      {                                                 \n        \"name\": \"films\",\n        \"columns\": [    \n          {\"name\": \"title\", \"type\": \"TEXT\"},\n          {\"name\": \"director\", \"type\": \"TEXT\"},                                                                  \n          {\"name\": \"release_year\", \"type\": \"INTEGER\"}\n        ]                                                                                                        \n      }                                                                                                          \n    ]\n  }                                                                                                              \n                                                        \n  Acceptance criteria:\n  - curl http://localhost:8000/schema returns valid JSON matching the shape above.\n  - Endpoint is documented in API_DOCUMENTATION.md.                                                              \n  - No changes to existing endpoints.",
